SUMMARY:[SM] Friends of Edgewood Natural Preserve: Weed Warriors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T120000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:flowstobay-17758-1793350800-1793361600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come help the California Native Plant Society’s Edgewood Wee
 d Warriors program and protect Edgewood’s amazing biodiversity by contro
 lling and removing invasive\, non-native plants. We’ll have great opport
 unities to see native wildflowers and other plants\, and to learn about lo
 cal ecology from other volunteers and local experts.Teens are welcome\, bu
 t must each be accompanied by one of their own parents\; unaccompanied adu
 lt students must have proof of age. Friday sessions run year round… meet
 ing locations are determined weekly\, so contact us for more information (
 or join our email contact list). For more info and contact details go to h
 ttps://friendsofedgewood.org/habitat-restoration. \nEWW operates by permit
  from County Parks… please don’t do any weeding on your own! \nLocatio
 n: Edgewood County Park & Natural Preserve in San Mateo County. \nSIGN UP 
 HERE\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. Confirm with even
 t host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/friends-of-edgewood-natur
 al-preserve-weed-warriors-2026-10-30/\nLast synced: 2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:Edgewood County Park & Natural Preserve\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/friends-of-edgewood-natural-preserve-w
 eed-warriors-2026-10-30/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] Friends of Edgewood Road Warriors: Adopt-A-Highway Workday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T120000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:flowstobay-17756-1793523600-1793534400@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Adopt-A-Highway\n\n\nRoad Warriors\nThe Friends of Edgewood or
 ganization has adopted a 1.7-mile stretch of northbound I-280 adjacent to 
 Edgewood Park. This segment was originally adopted in 1989 by Ken Seydel\,
  who graciously transferred responsibility to the Friends of Edgewood in 1
 998. Ken served as program coordinator until 2014 and continues as to part
 icipate as a volunteer. \nThe Adopt-A-Highway group meets at the Edgewood 
 Road / I-280 Park & Ride lot in the morning of the first Saturday of even-
 numbered months and the first Sunday of odd-numbered (schedule changes are
  made due to holidays and weather). Work teams disperse along the adopted 
 area to bag litter and move debris to collection points. \nFor further inf
 ormation about the Friends of Edgewood Adopt-A-Highway program\, contact D
 ave Hershey at road-warriors-coord@friendsofedgewood.org. Adopt-A-Highway
  is conducted in cooperation with Caltrans\, which provides instructions\,
  safety training\, and equipment.\n\nAges: Varies per event — many famil
 y-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calen
 dar/friends-of-edgewood-road-warriors-adopt-a-highway-workday-2026-11-01/
 \nLast synced: 2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:Edgewood County Park & Natural Preserve\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/friends-of-edgewood-road-warriors-adop
 t-a-highway-workday-2026-11-01/
END:VEVENT
